# What the sdist carries beyond the wheel.
#
# The wheel's contents are decided by [tool.setuptools.package-data] in
# pyproject.toml and are already right: the engine sources, the corpus, the
# skill and the hooks. This file exists for the one thing a *source*
# distribution has to do that a wheel does not — be built and checked from —
# and for one thing setuptools gets wrong on its own.
#
# The wrong thing first: setuptools sweeps `tests/test_*.py` into the sdist by
# name and leaves `tests/conftest.py` behind, so an unpacked sdist collects 500+
# tests and then dies on the first fixture. A test suite that ships broken is
# worse than one that does not ship.

include Makefile
include CHANGELOG.md CLAUDE.md
recursive-include docs *.md

# `make test` and `make conformance` are the two gates a downstream packager
# runs before trusting a build, and both need the tree rather than the package.
# Named by extension rather than `graft tests`: a graft also takes
# `tests/__pycache__` — a quarter of a megabyte of .pyc in every sdist built
# from a tree anyone has run pytest in, which then needs a `global-exclude` to
# take back out, which warns four times per build about matching nothing.
recursive-include tests *.py
recursive-include tests/corpus *.jsonl

# Defence, not decoration. `include_package_data = true` means anything named
# here under src/ lands in the *wheel* too, and these three directories are
# where cargo and the MicroPython make put hundreds of megabytes of object
# files. Nothing above names them today; these lines are what stops a future
# `graft src` from shipping a gigabyte to everyone who types `pip install`.
prune src/lypning/assets/rust/target
prune src/lypning/assets/micropython/build
prune src/lypning/assets/micropython/.build
